WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.677
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel. Welcome to Online Upper-Intermediate.

2
00:00:04.977 --> 00:00:08.108
Hi! I'm Nita. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.408 --> 00:00:14.114
Unit thirteen: The Art of Persuasion. In this unit, you will argue, persuade and emphasise your point.

4
00:00:15.117 --> 00:00:15.886
debate.

5
00:00:16.586 --> 00:00:20.396
debate means a formal discussion where people argue different views.

6
00:00:20.696 --> 00:00:23.416
Our class held a debate on school uniforms.

7
00:00:24.116 --> 00:00:26.211
Your turn. Say: debate.

8
00:00:28.911 --> 00:00:29.761
debate.

9
00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:31.728
convince.

10
00:00:32.428 --> 00:00:34.694
convince means to make someone believe something.

11
00:00:34.994 --> 00:00:36.866
She convinced me to join the club.

12
00:00:37.566 --> 00:00:39.661
Your turn. Say: convince.

13
00:00:42.361 --> 00:00:43.362
convince.

14
00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:45.247
rhetoric.

15
00:00:45.947 --> 00:00:49.432
rhetoric means persuasive language, sometimes without real meaning.

16
00:00:49.732 --> 00:00:52.254
The politician's speech was full of rhetoric.

17
00:00:52.954 --> 00:00:55.363
Your turn. Say: rhetoric.

18
00:00:58.063 --> 00:00:58.925
rhetoric.

19
00:00:59.917 --> 00:01:01.231
evidence-based.

20
00:01:01.931 --> 00:01:05.173
evidence-based means supported by facts and research.

21
00:01:05.473 --> 00:01:07.484
We need evidence-based policies.

22
00:01:08.184 --> 00:01:10.546
Your turn. Say: evidence-based.

23
00:01:13.246 --> 00:01:14.584
evidence-based.

24
00:01:15.583 --> 00:01:16.445
point of view.

25
00:01:17.145 --> 00:01:19.145
point of view means a personal opinion.

26
00:01:19.445 --> 00:01:21.700
I understand your point of view, but I disagree.

27
00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:24.588
Your turn. Say: point of view.

28
00:01:27.288 --> 00:01:28.265
point of view.

29
00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:30.019
logical.

30
00:01:30.719 --> 00:01:33.833
logical means reasonable and based on clear thinking.

31
00:01:34.133 --> 00:01:36.109
Her argument was clear and logical.

32
00:01:36.809 --> 00:01:39.253
Your turn. Say: logical.

33
00:01:41.953 --> 00:01:42.954
logical.

34
00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:45.207
emotional appeal.

35
00:01:45.907 --> 00:01:49.764
emotional appeal means trying to persuade by making people feel something.

36
00:01:50.064 --> 00:01:52.528
Charity adverts often use emotional appeal.

37
00:01:53.228 --> 00:01:55.729
Your turn. Say: emotional appeal.

38
00:01:58.429 --> 00:01:59.871
emotional appeal.

39
00:02:00.883 --> 00:02:02.117
compromise solution.

40
00:02:02.817 --> 00:02:06.372
compromise solution means an answer where both sides give up something.

41
00:02:06.672 --> 00:02:08.660
They agreed on a compromise solution.

42
00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:11.943
Your turn. Say: compromise solution.

43
00:02:14.643 --> 00:02:16.096
compromise solution.

44
00:02:17.083 --> 00:02:18.967
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:19.267 --> 00:02:21.858
What convinced you to vote for the new school policy?

46
00:02:23.150 --> 00:02:27.242
What convinced me was the evidence. The argument was really logical.

47
00:02:28.550 --> 00:02:30.677
Wasn't there a lot of rhetoric in the debate?

48
00:02:31.983 --> 00:02:36.584
Yes, but it was the data that changed my point of view, not the emotional appeal.

49
00:02:37.883 --> 00:02:39.059
And the other side?

50
00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:44.497
What they wanted was a compromise solution, and that's what we finally agreed on.

51
00:02:45.783 --> 00:02:48.990
Grammar focus: Cleft sentences for emphasis.

52
00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:52.776
Use cleft sentences to emphasise the most important information.

53
00:02:53.076 --> 00:02:56.596
What plus clause plus is, or it was plus focus plus that.

54
00:02:56.896 --> 00:03:01.940
For example: What convinced me was the evidence. It was the data that changed my mind.

55
00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:06.864
Cleft sentences are useful in speeches and debates to highlight your key point.

56
00:03:07.850 --> 00:03:11.025
Now read and listen. Ethos, Pathos and Logos.

57
00:03:11.325 --> 00:03:16.273
Over two thousand years ago, Aristotle described three ways to persuade people.

58
00:03:17.583 --> 00:03:22.125
Ethos is about trust: what matters is whether the speaker seems reliable.

59
00:03:23.417 --> 00:03:27.599
Pathos is emotional appeal, which moves the audience's feelings.

60
00:03:28.883 --> 00:03:31.812
Logos is logical, evidence-based reasoning.

61
00:03:33.117 --> 00:03:36.637
It is the combination of all three that makes a speech truly convincing.

62
00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:40.393
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:40.693 --> 00:03:44.365
Persuasive language, sometimes without real meaning, is blank.

64
00:03:44.665 --> 00:03:47.842
A, rhetoric. B, debate. C, evidence.

65
00:03:51.850 --> 00:03:53.733
The answer is A: rhetoric.

66
00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:57.075
blank I need is a long holiday.

67
00:03:57.375 --> 00:04:00.065
A, That. B, What. C, Which.

68
00:04:04.050 --> 00:04:05.365
The answer is B: What.

69
00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:09.291
It was my teacher blank encouraged me to apply.

70
00:04:09.591 --> 00:04:12.606
A, what. B, that. C, which.

71
00:04:16.617 --> 00:04:18.372
The answer is B: that.

72
00:04:19.883 --> 00:04:22.603
An answer where both sides give up something is a blank.

73
00:04:22.903 --> 00:04:27.299
A, point of view. B, compromise solution. C, emotional appeal.

74
00:04:31.283 --> 00:04:33.817
The answer is B: compromise solution.

75
00:04:35.317 --> 00:04:37.688
According to the text, logos means blank.

76
00:04:37.988 --> 00:04:41.154
A, trust. B, emotion. C, logical reasoning.

77
00:04:45.150 --> 00:04:47.312
The answer is C: logical reasoning.

78
00:04:48.817 --> 00:04:53.094
Now it's your turn to speak. Try to convince me that learning English is important.

79
00:04:58.394 --> 00:05:04.634
What really matters is opportunity. It's English that opens doors to better jobs, travel and knowledge.

80
00:05:04.934 --> 00:05:06.504
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:07.517 --> 00:05:12.154
Great work today! You learned eight new words and cleft sentences for emphasis.

82
00:05:12.454 --> 00:05:15.896
Today's value is respect. Thank the people who help us.

83
00:05:16.196 --> 00:05:18.477
See you in Unit fourteen. Goodbye!

84
00:05:18.777 --> 00:05:21.511
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

